<title>USA: Former AMA head to join tobaco talks - WSJ.</title>
<headline>Former AMA head to join tobaco talks - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Officials from leading public health groups have chosen Lonnie Bristow, the former president of the American Medical Association, to join the tobacco industry's settlement talks, the Wall Street Journal said on Monday's electronic edition.</p>
<p>The Journal said the move could give more legitimacy to the anti-tobacco negotiating team, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Bristow was not immediately available for comment, the paper said.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
